<title>USA: NTSB's Hall gives priority to collison avoidance.</title>
<headline>NTSB's Hall gives priority to collison avoidance.</headline>
<byline>Teresa Carson</byline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collision avoidance equipment on cargo aircraft is a top safety priority for the National Transportation Safety Board, the chairman told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Traffic Alert and Collision Avoidance System (TCAS) is the most wanted item we have regarding cargo aircraft,&quot; James Hall, chairman of the National Transportation Safety Board said Monday.     TCAS is the primary type of aircraft collision</p>
<p>avoidance equipment. It is currently required on commercial passenger aircraft in the United States, but not on cargo aircraft.</p>
</text>
